      </Main>
      <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>By air sealing and adding an HRV you could also be eligible for a $5000 Yukon Good Energy Rebate.

To qualify for the air sealing rebate:

    your home must have at least 3 air changes per hour as determined by the initial energy assessment;
    you must have 1.5 or fewer air changes per hour @50 Pascals (Pa) post-renovation; and
    you must install an HRV to ensure balanced ventilation in your home. See Upgrades and renovations: heat-recovery ventilator (HRV) in the rebates list.

The air sealing rebate is issued when the building achieves or exceeds the air sealing target.
</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>
The insulation rebate amount for above-ground walls is based on the percentage of the total wall area youve insulated. For example, if you insulate 50 per cent of your homes total above-ground walls, youll receive $6,000. If you insulate 100 per cent of your homes total above-ground walls, youll re-ceive $12,000.
To qualify for the insulation rebate for above-ground walls, you must at least double the existing insula-tion level. For example, if the original insulation value is R20, you must increase the insulation to R40 or greater.
</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>You are also eligible for a $2500 Good Energy insulation rebate if you increase the attic insulation to R-60 or better.

To qualify for the attic insulation rebate:

    the insulation level must be R40 or less prior to the renovation; and
    you must increase it to R60 or greater.

For attics with rafters or low-heel trusses, the insulation level may be as low as R20 at the eaves as long as it increases to R60 within 1.2 metres of the eaves.

You must insulate the entire attic. You can apply for the attic insulation rebate only once per building.
</ceilings>
                <foundation>To receive the insulation rebate for slabs or floor systems:

   the insulation level must be R20 or less prior to the renovation; and
   you must increase it by at least R20.
</foundation>
                <windows>You are also eligible for an additional $125 per window through the Good Energy
window rebate.

This rebate is for upgrades completed in an existing residence. A residence that is 5 years or older is considered an existing residence.

All windows must be new and ENERGY STAR®-certified.

Sealed or insulated glass window units are not eligible for this rebate.

The windows installed must be for residential use only.
A maximum of 15 windows per existing home are eligible.
Used products are not eligible.
</windows>
                <HeatingSystem>You are also eligible for a Good Energy rebate of 40% of project costs, up to a
maximum of $8,000 for the installation of a ducted system or mini- or multi-split air
source heat pump system. Rebates are based on equipment costs, labour, electrical
upgrades, construction costs and/or contracting and professional expenses related to
the installation and supporting infrastructure.
</HeatingSystem>
                <AdditionalComments>Programs in your region that you may be eligible for include:
Good Energy Program website: 
https://yukon.ca/good-energy

E-rebate portal direct link
https://yukon.myenergyxpert.com/

</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
